      "content": "it's a decent start, but it feels a bit thin on the actual \"citizen\" aspect. the tracker is pretty strict, and while we don't want it to be a joke, that first draft's score is going to be way too low to even clear the initial threshold. \n\ncan you beef up the section? try to integrate the concept of the \"citizen\" more thoroughly throughout the whole thing—maybe link it to civic engagement, rights to green space, or individual wellbeing. just please, please don't just list the word over and over in a way that's obvious. make it sound like a sophisticated urban planning argument where \"citizen\" is a key thematic element. we need a higher score to get past the bot, but it still has to pass the human sniff test.",
